VERDICT: needs-changes
{"verdict":"needs-changes","summary":"I now agree the narrowed clear is not safe: in the shrink path `set_height` does not scroll older native-scrollback content back onto rows `[0, top)`, so those rows retain the old screen contents while the same history tail is redrawn lower down. This can leave stale/duplicated transcript rows above the viewport rather than a correctly repainted or intentionally blank region.","concede":["I drop my prior approval of the comment’s premise that rows `[0, top)` necessarily contain terminal-scrolled content that must be preserved; the shrink path only clears the old viewport and moves `viewport.y`, it does not perform a scroll that would populate those rows with the older committed history lines."],"maintain":["The `scrollback_committed` clamp is still necessary to avoid redrawing native-scrollback lines and creating scrollback duplication; the issue is specifically that skipping the clear for the unredrawn prefix leaves stale visible rows after the viewport moves down."],"findings":[{"file":"crates/mu-solo/src/viewport.rs","line":651,"severity":"high","issue":"Changing the clear loop to `top..visible_rows` leaves rows `[0, top)` untouched when `scrollback_committed > naive_start`. In the shrink path, no terminal scroll operation repopulates those rows with older committed history; they retain the previous screen contents while `history[start..]` is redrawn starting at `top`, producing stale/duplicated rows above the viewport."}]}
